WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.680
Everyone has heard the stories about what
happened back in ‘68.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.310
The most brutal series of occult murders in
Wyoming history: Ten victims killed over a

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:16.880
series of four months, found with their hearts
cut out near some old cabin out in the sticks.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.019
All these innocent people’s lives were cut
short in the service of worshipping some entity

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:24.000
that nobody else understood.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.550
Thankfully, the murders had stopped by the
start of the seventies, and this humble Wyoming

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.060
county knew nothing but peace for several
years after.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.579
But the cabin where it all happened remained
abandoned.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:40.240
The ground was sour there; weighed down by
the horrors that’d transpired.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.980
You’d need to be brave or foolish to set
foot there, all things considered.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.941
That’s what led 17-year-old Charlie and
his reluctant girlfriend, Samantha, to that

00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:53.530
rickety old building one cold, dark winter
night.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.949
He was doing what most foolhardy teenage boys
tried to do with almost every action they

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:00.289
took: Prove himself.

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:04.180
Samantha was just along for the ride, despite
her protests.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.060
Her folks had always warned her about this
place.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.990
The word they most often used to describe
it was, “Evil.”

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.230
But Charlie wouldn’t take no for an answer.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:19.540
He was going to open that rickety front door
and step inside, and Samantha would watch,

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.510
in awe of his bravery.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:27.580
Though as he got closer, and felt his fingers
nearing the door handle, a pang of fear tingled

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.700
through him.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.040
Was this really something he wanted to do?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.400
Too late to back out now, Samantha was watching.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.130
He couldn’t be a coward.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.780
He needed to commit.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.440
He needed to prove he could do this.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.590
Charlie took a final deep breath, opened the
door, and stepped through into the dark.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.240
He would never be seen again.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.670
Samantha squinted and looked into the dark.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.660
There was no “into”, really.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.180
It was almost like a giant, black rectangle
was obscuring the doorway.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.980
There was no way to make out any of the features
inside.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.340
She called her boyfriend’s name with a quivering
voice and got nothing in response.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.730
That’s when she should have started running.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.090
It might have even saved her.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.720
A figure emerged from the door, walking fast.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.630
It was solid black, with no discernable features,
only a vaguely humanoid shape.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.450
It walked towards her with such speed and
purpose that poor Samantha didn’t even have

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.920
time to scream.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.720
The creature extended a clawed hand, and reached
through her chest - It didn’t even break

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.730
the skin, just phased through her skin, muscle,
and bone like a ghost passing through a wall.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.940
Suddenly, she felt immense pain as the creature
drew back its hand.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.150
It was holding something that moved and squirmed
in its clawed grip.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:48.970
It was only as Samantha collapsed, her vision
going dark for the last time, that she realized

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.980
she was looking at her own, beating heart.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.880
And this wouldn’t be where the horrors ended
for this little Wyoming town.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.010
No, this was only the beginning.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:02.220
More people would go missing in the following
days and weeks.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.030
Wildlife and livestock would also be found
dead under mysterious circumstances.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:11.960
Local vets were baffled by dead pets found
in yards with no obvious cause of death, only

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.720
to be confused and horrified when they performed
an autopsy and found massive internal bleeding,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.860
and a missing heart.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.770
Despite the fact that there was never any
kind of wound indicating a heart’s removal.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.970
Your average weird occult murders are the
FBI’s problem, but when hearts start to

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:34.410
disappear in a mysterious fashion, that’s
how the SCP Foundation gets involved in your

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.410
case.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.250
They dispatched a number of Field Agents into
the town in order to track down the source

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:44.150
of this anomalous activity, and potentially
secure and contain whatever hostile entity

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.470
was behind it.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:51.440
In this case, they really didn’t need to
track the entity down: It came for them.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.180
Three agents were driving down a lonely Wyoming
road near the cabin when a sudden series of

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.400
shapes glowed into prominence in the car’s
high beams.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.780
It wasn’t just one of those vantablack creatures,
it was several.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.760
The second the car ground to a halt, the entities
engaged with extreme hostility.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.920
They attacked, seeming unaffected by conventional
arms fire from the two agents in the front

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.920
seats.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.630
They dragged them out of the car, before reaching
into their chests and pulling out their hearts.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.350
The agent in the back seat got lucky.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:25.940
He’d had experience with beings similar
to this in the past, and had one method that

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.210
might work.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:32.590
As they drew towards him, he loaded a magazine
of silver-tipped rounds into his handgun.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.770
Closer, closer.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:39.680
The agent also happened to be a devout Muslim,
and as the creatures approached, he drew his

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.300
weapon and prayed to Allah for the strength
to overcome these demons.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.530
He opened fire, just as they were climbing
into the car and reaching for him.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.970
For the first time, the bullets seemed to
have an effect.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.250
The creatures squealed as the gunfire rendered
through them.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:05:00.030
The ones dealt fatal wounds briefly convulsed,
before melting into a fine, sulphuric sludge.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.490
The agent, thinking on his feet, noticed that
the creatures that stole the hearts of his

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.330
two fellow agents were fleeing.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:09.150
He followed them, trying to find their source.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.000
And of course, it was the cabin.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.750
The creatures passed back through the open
door, into the darkness of the cabin.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.980
How many of them were there?

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.240
And what was going on inside?

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:25.710
Naturally, the full might of the SCP Foundation
rolled into town not long after this incident.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:32.780
Knowing now that the cabin - designated SCP-1983-1
- was the source of the creatures - designated

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:37.590
SCP-1983-2 - things were easier to get under
control.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:42.780
A fake chemical plant was built around the
cabin as a pretense to keep it contained - this

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.430
plant became known as Outpost 54.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.380
On-site researchers would sleep in the facility;
soldiers required for the regular culling

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:55.430
of 1983-2 instances would make their home
in the barracks.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:06:00.530
And of course, there was also a large armory
filled with the specialized weaponry and ammunition

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.560
required to put the rampaging, heart-stealing
creatures down.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.970
The fateful encounter that the surviving agent
had with these aggressive entities provided

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:15.520
the Foundation with an invaluable piece of
data on how to combat SCP-1983.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:21.669
For reasons not fully understood, the 1983-2
creatures have an extreme reaction against

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:23.430
sincere human belief.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:29.090
It doesn’t matter which religion you personally
follow, if you’re a true believer, and you

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.830
make a prayer to your deity of choice while
firing on one of these monsters with silver-based

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.460
ammunition, you will be able to slay them.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.920
Brings a whole new meaning to the phrase “spray
and pray.”

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.300
But the belief must be truly sincere for the
attack to work.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.810
If there is doubt or skepticism in your heart
when you’re praying and firing, well, let’s

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.280
just say it won’t be your heart for much
longer…

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:57.190
These very particular killing methods are
the reason that MTF Chi-13, also known as

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:01.950
The Choir Boys, were brought in to be the
personal stewards of 1983’s containment.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:07.169
They’re a Mobile Task Force formed entirely
of devout religious believers, whose faith

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:13.889
girds them against the influences of a number
of occult monsters - SCP-1983 included.

00:07:13.889 --> 00:07:17.950
The Foundation performed a series of cursory
tests on the cabin itself.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.340
The building contained several frustrating
spatial anomalies, with the locus of these

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.979
being the front door, and the living room
behind it.

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:30.570
The living room seemed impossible to access
by any means other than the anomalous aperture

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.370
in the front door.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:36.550
Any attempts to enter via the wall, or other
doors in the house, simply cause the researchers

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.889
to pop up in different areas of the house.

00:07:39.889 --> 00:07:44.170
After a barrage of tests, including busting
holes in the exterior walls in an attempt

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:49.800
to enter - to no avail, of course - the O5
Council forbade further testing.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:55.090
It simply wasn’t worth potentially creating
more openings that 1983-2 instances could

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.509
emerge from.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:08:02.389
This left only one option: Launching excursions
into the heart of the anomaly itself via the

00:08:02.389 --> 00:08:04.710
portal in the front door.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:09.110
This seemed to be the only way to successfully
gather intel about the inner workings.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.350
For the first of three fateful incidents,
a detachment from the Choir Boys, armed with

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:16.160
silver munitions, was sent into the portal.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:21.419
None of them ever returned, but for the first
time in years, the front door mysteriously

00:08:21.419 --> 00:08:23.030
closed again.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:29.220
This led to a drastic reduction in the release
of SCP-1983-2 instances, but still left a

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:31.840
whole team potentially stranded inside.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:37.170
A second detachment from the Choir Boys was
prepared to head in and, if not rescue, at

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.560
least find out what happened to the first.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:44.619
They opened the door and ventured inside,
only for history to repeat itself.

00:08:44.619 --> 00:08:47.680
Not one of them would ever be seen alive again.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.690
And what’s more, with the door once again
open, another one of the entities soon charged

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:56.179
out and began attacking more Foundation researchers.

00:08:56.179 --> 00:09:01.459
The onslaught only stopped with the brave
sacrifice of Agent Morris, a field agent stationed

00:09:01.459 --> 00:09:03.879
at Outpost 54 at the time.

00:09:03.879 --> 00:09:08.339
He entered the doorway and closed the door
once again from the inside.

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:13.110
Just like everyone else, Agent Morris was
sadly never seen alive again.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:18.290
But on May 23, 1989, something remarkable
happened.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:22.970
Having wasted too many agents on this anomaly
already, the Foundation decided to send in

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.309
a D-Class.

00:09:24.309 --> 00:09:29.139
The D-Class in question was Jackson Parker,
a man whose personnel file indicated he had

00:09:29.139 --> 00:09:34.000
a profound belief in the moral fairness of
the universe - that everything that happened

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.779
simply must have happened for a reason, even
his own incarceration.

00:09:38.779 --> 00:09:43.740
He was given a camera with a live feed, and
a lifeline leading back outside, before practically

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.000
being pushed into the cabin.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.110
Moments later, the lifeline was pulled taut
and snapped.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.059
The feed cut off at around the same time.

00:09:52.059 --> 00:09:56.410
Foundation researchers at the outpost sighed,
having lost another guinea pig.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.869
Little did they know, Jackson Parker wasn’t
dead.

00:09:59.869 --> 00:10:05.949
And what’s more, he was about to do what
no agent of the SCP Foundation could: Destroy

00:10:05.949 --> 00:10:09.009
SCP-1983.

00:10:09.009 --> 00:10:12.209
On the inside, Jackson was met with a nightmare.

00:10:12.209 --> 00:10:16.559
This anomaly was so much worse than anyone
knew: It didn’t look like the inside of

00:10:16.559 --> 00:10:22.110
a cabin, it was a surreal shadow dimension,
looking like a patchwork amalgamation of so

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:30.029
many different buildings: Hospitals, schools,
offices, homes, factories, military installations.

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:34.810
Jackson even recognized the dingy basement
of his childhood home among the chaos.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:41.980
At that moment, it was clear - This wasn’t
just one anomalous location, it was the nexus

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:44.120
point for many.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:49.430
How many doors were there out there, in how
many different buildings, unleashing the horrors

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:51.429
of SCP-1983?

00:10:51.429 --> 00:10:52.769
Across the world?

00:10:52.769 --> 00:10:54.870
Across dimensions, even?

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.989
Lucky for Jackson, he was about to receive
a little help from beyond the grave.

00:10:58.989 --> 00:11:03.329
One of the Choir Boys, Agent Barclay, had
written a note before he died.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:08.889
Here, he gave the few pieces of information
Jackson needed not only to survive but potentially

00:11:08.889 --> 00:11:11.350
even destroy this thing once and for all.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:17.019
First, that the entities, born from shadows,
are weaker in the dark - light gives them

00:11:17.019 --> 00:11:19.560
form, in the dark, they’re intangible.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:24.920
Second, there is no way out through the front
door: If someone tries to escape outside,

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:28.269
their body will melt almost instantaneously.

00:11:28.269 --> 00:11:33.300
And most importantly of all, Agent Barclay
realized why they’d been taking the hearts:

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:38.550
In the center of this terrible place lies
The Nest, a giant pile of human hearts surrounded

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:42.279
by light sources, acting as a kind of incubator.

00:11:42.279 --> 00:11:48.660
After being placed in the nest, the hearts
burst open, and new instances of SCP-1983-2

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.290
emerge.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:57.439
If someone could destroy The Nest, it may
destroy the very heart of SCP-1983, and finally

00:11:57.439 --> 00:11:59.809
neutralize this nightmarish anomaly.

00:11:59.809 --> 00:12:04.100
Agent Barclay had lost his faith seeing his
friends slaughtered around him, so he didn’t

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.769
have it in himself to finish this thing.

00:12:06.769 --> 00:12:09.369
It could only be Jackson now.

00:12:09.369 --> 00:12:14.290
And as you know, Jackson had an unshakable
belief that everything happens for a reason.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:18.749
Perhaps the reason he was here was to finally
bring an end to the suffering, and that’s

00:12:18.749 --> 00:12:21.699
exactly what he was going to do.

00:12:21.699 --> 00:12:25.389
Jackson shouldered Barclay’s rifle, and
charged through the labyrinth, gunning down

00:12:25.389 --> 00:12:29.579
attacking SCP-1983-2 entities on the way.

00:12:29.579 --> 00:12:31.339
He was a man on a mission.

00:12:31.339 --> 00:12:37.410
Soon, he made his way into the central chamber
and finally saw it: The Nest, this horrifying

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.170
pile of wriggling human hearts.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:43.369
One of the many sights that finally broke
Agent Barclay.

00:12:43.369 --> 00:12:46.269
But Jackson stood unbroken.

00:12:46.269 --> 00:12:50.820
He aimed the rifle at The Nest and opened
fire, the sheer force of his unshakable belief

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.489
super-charging his every shot.

00:12:53.489 --> 00:12:59.730
He had struck a killing blow at the heart
of the beast, avenging everyone it ever murdered.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:04.660
On the outside, to everyone’s amazement,
SCP-1983 disappeared.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.559
The front door opened and the darkness dissipated
within.

00:13:08.559 --> 00:13:12.829
When agents and researchers entered, they
found the desiccated corpses of several Mobile

00:13:12.829 --> 00:13:17.619
Task Force members, but all signs of the previous
anomaly were gone.

00:13:17.619 --> 00:13:21.910
From the same note left on the corpse of Agent
Barclay, it was clear to the researchers that

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:28.490
Jackson Parker had taken the advice, and finally
neutralized this dangerous Keter-Class anomaly.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:33.019
Though Jackson himself was nowhere to be found,
he was given a posthumous medal of bravery

00:13:33.019 --> 00:13:37.399
and merit by the Foundation - Only one of
two ever awarded to a D-Class.

00:13:37.399 --> 00:13:42.240
I guess you could say that everything happens
for a reason.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:47.379
Now go check out “SCP-3999 - I Am At The
Center of Everything That Happens To Me”

00:13:47.379 --> 00:13:52.839
and “SCP-5049 - The Skin Salesman - Demon
Dan's Discount Homunculus Depot” for more

00:13:52.839 --> 00:13:56.360
explorations into the hearts of genuinely
unnerving SCPs!

